  "Number": 18,
  "Question": "Of the following sets, the one that includes all values of \\(x\\) which will satisfy \\(2x-3\\gt7-x\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x\\gt4\\)",
    "B": "\\(x\\lt\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(x=\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(x\\gt\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(x\\lt0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Add \\(x+3\\) to both sides to collect the variable terms on the left and the constants on the right:\n\\[\n2x-3>7-x\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n3x>10.\n\\]\nDividing by the positive number \\(3\\) preserves the inequality's direction, giving\n\\[\n\\boxed{x>\\frac{10}{3}}.\n\\]\nAll the steps are reversible, so this describes every solution. The endpoint \\(10/3\\) is excluded because the original inequality is strict. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
